hacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖v‖=7$ and $‖2u+v‖=25.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖u‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c8d5431f2416a11a2ffd140598219391744997246558f294f0abd839312a40a" "basis" 1467 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $2u$ is orthogonal to $v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+v{‖}^{2} & =‖2u{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+v{‖}^{2} & =(2‖u‖)^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖2u+v{‖}^{2} & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (25)^{2} & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+(7)^{2} \\\\ 625 & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+49 \\\\ 576 & =4‖u{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖u{‖}^{2} & =144\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖u‖=12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c8d5431f2416a11a2ffd140598219391744997246558f294f0abd839312a40a" "basis" 1467 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc" "basi