lso have that $u$ is orthogonal to $2v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+2v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+‖2v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+2v{‖}^{2} & =‖u‖+(‖2v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖u+2v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (6\\sqrt{6})^{2} & =(6\\sqrt{2})^{2}+4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 216 & =72+4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 144 & =4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖v{‖}^{2} & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖v‖=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048257/state.json" "file_sha256" "797dff20b4319f1b37405a7d50b7088a0d980fa80dd36e79e0dabf7a44fee50d"} {"question" "q-40263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048257/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e2f7c011c28a30d158917074d36797a8cff9e5991a121e9ce0a158de43205903"} {"question" "q-40263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048257/state.json" "file_sha256" "797dff20b4319f1b37405a7d50b7088a0d980fa80dd36e79e0dabf7a44fee50d"} {"question" "q-40263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{6}"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048257/state.json" "file_sha256" "797dff20b4319f1b37405a7d50b7088a0d980fa80dd36e79e0dabf7a44fee50d"} {"question" "q-40263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/